# The paths only the tech lead changes (AGENTS.md, rules 1 and 2).
# GitHub shows the owner on a pull request that touches one of them.
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# A leading slash anchors a path at the repository root. The last matching
# line wins.
#
# infra/ is left out until the directory exists. Add it in the task that
# scaffolds it.

/.github/ @sophophilix
/.claude/ @sophophilix
/tools/sdlc/ @sophophilix
/bin/sdlc @sophophilix
/docs/decisions/ @sophophilix
/pnpm-lock.yaml @sophophilix
/pnpm-workspace.yaml @sophophilix

# The rest of the kit (AGENTS.md, rule 2).
/AGENTS.md @sophophilix
/CLAUDE.md @sophophilix
/Makefile @sophophilix
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @sophophilix

# The files that waive a scanner finding. Some of them don't exist yet.
# gitleaks loads its two from a pull request's own tree, so the owner line
# must exist before the file does. zizmor loads its configuration the same
# way, from the repository root or from .github/, which is owned above.
/osv-scanner.toml @sophophilix
/.gitleaks.toml @sophophilix
/.gitleaksignore @sophophilix
/zizmor.yml @sophophilix
/zizmor.yaml @sophophilix
/docs/security/accepted-advisories.md @sophophilix
